# An allow-list (bead contextbroker-3xd): the API image carries only what the running API and the
# commands run inside it import, so an untracked file in the working tree (telemetry.log, seed_data/,
# .env.example, stop_context.sh, a scratch directory) can never reach the image. The library-only packages
# (governance_gate, action_lifecycle, decision_records, investigation_workers, loop_coordination and the
# two empty ones) stay in the repository with their tests but are not listed here, so they are left out
# too (bead contextbroker-c8g). tests/test_unwired_packages.py pins that every package the runtime imports
# is listed and that none of those is.
*
!requirements.txt
!broker.py
!seed_graph.py
!agent_harness
!artefact_governance
!broker_engine
!broker_state
!data_contracts
!ingestion
!intent_management
!okf_retrieval
!outcome_assurance
!state_reconciliation
!ontologies
# Inside ontologies: the licensed ontology material, other TBox files and the operator's binding files stay out.
ontologies/licensed
**/ontology/**/*.ttl
ontologies/tbox/*.ttl
!ontologies/tbox/topology.ttl
ontologies/abox/*.ttl
!ontologies/abox/topology-demo.ttl
ontologies/**/*.zip
# Named again on purpose: tracker, planning, design notes, scripts, the knowledge files (mounted read-only,
# never copied), the optional MCP extra and the licensed documents stay out even if the allow-list changes.
.beads/
.planning/
.claude/
design/
scripts/
knowledge/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
planning.md
requirements-mcp.txt
requirements-mcp.in
docs/spec/TR29*.pdf
docs/spec/TMF921*.pdf
# Never in an image, wherever they sit.
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
*.pem
*.key
.env
